If a pregnant-person has an undue-travel-burden for a neonatal-opioid-withdrawal-prepared-facility then every clinician should arrange a local-delivery for the pregnant-person.
If a clinician arranges a local-delivery for a pregnant-person and the pregnant-person has a newborn then the clinician should monitor the newborn for a neonatal-opioid-withdrawal-syndrome and should evaluate the newborn for a neonatal-opioid-withdrawal-syndrome.
If a clinician monitors a newborn for a neonatal-opioid-withdrawal-syndrome and evaluates the newborn for the neonatal-opioid-withdrawal-syndrome and the newborn needs an additional-treatment then the clinician should transfer the newborn for the additional-treatment.
